    {
      "id": "claim_db078b64cc3243a29927fe9f4140a69b",
      "statement": "Approval policy is designed to evolve in three stages — hardcoded local list (current), configurable local policy, and enterprise policy API — with evaluation kept behind a small local requiresApproval-style function, while agent polling for approval status and a relay-side in-memory status registry are explicitly out of scope for this stage so the MCP server remains stateless across per-invocation processes.",
