    {
      "id": "claim_05ae3386cb7b418cb30cda57abfab7b7",
      "statement": "Explicit non-goals marked intentionally unsupported in the capability matrix include no cookie/browser-storage export, no session cloning, no browser mirroring/remote desktop, no continuous screenshots, no continuous DOM streaming, no background surveillance, no browser-history collection, no credential extraction (password fields return browser_error), and no MFA interception; implemented security properties include user-controlled bridge activation, pairing-token authentication, the explicit request/response model, and no background data transmission (keepalives carry no browser state).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/project/CAPABILITY_MATRIX.md#L146-L159",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b57286d5c2b7860439024195b4f3d1de14b74c8409f0a5dd79b177e9643a48db:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/security/SECURITY_GUARANTEES.md#L6-L73",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:af078247ec44343a08a539b8cb36077fb917ae09c61c00a04fb7f4c4ff2feaf1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_38c5f9f29a8848dcb74c73ba9ac44286",
      "statement": "AGENTS.md defines non-negotiable change constraints tied to security: no continuous page/DOM/screenshot/history/browser-state streaming, no silent background surveillance, cookie export, credential extraction, session cloning, or MFA interception; no persisting page content unless an accepted ADR requires it; preserve authenticated private browser/tab routing with explicit request IDs, structured errors, and timeouts; preserve user-visible connection state and configured client-side action approval without bypassing approval checks; keep permissions minimal and document why each is needed; and prefer progressive disclosure.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://AGENTS.md#L48-L82",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7f0fe34782c315929110695bbb954da3cb7a8de324f58453b72b1445161a434d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9f3945e3b7e2412caf904f755e3f908c",
      "statement": "Planned security hardening on the roadmap (status Planned) includes end-to-end encryption (relay cannot inspect payloads), fine-grained per-capability approvals before an agent can use a tool, and user-approval workflows for sensitive actions such as payments, deletions, and data exports.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/project/CAPABILITY_MATRIX.md#L225-L233",
